Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Stop subdividing degenerate overlapping control triangles.

Adapted from M3rocto's synthetic reproducer and withdrawn patch in:
https://github.com/marselnenaj/fenix-a320-linux-patch/pull/9
This loop has not been identified as the cause of the simulator display freeze.

Nearly coincident curves can remain overlapping after subdivision because of
floating-point rounding. Stop when both control triangles are tiny. Reject a
non-finite area on either side as well: comparing a finite area to NaN would
otherwise repeatedly select the NaN curve, without ever reducing the other.

The tolerance is absolute in path coordinates, before the world transform.
Also reject NaN line-intersection parameters before they create invalid path
vertices (Wine bug 51139). Ordered comparisons alone otherwise accept 0/0.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c
@@ -2274,7 +2274,7 @@
         t = (intersection.x - q[0]->x) / (q[1]->x - q[0]->x);
     else
         t = (intersection.y - q[0]->y) / (q[1]->y - q[0]->y);
-    if (t < 0.0f || t > 1.0f)
+    if (!(t >= 0.0f && t <= 1.0f))
         return TRUE;
 
     d2d_point_lerp(&intersection, q[0], q[1], t);
@@ -3419,7 +3419,17 @@
         {
             while (d2d_geometry_check_bezier_overlap(geometry, &idx_p, &idx_q))
             {
-                if (fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_q)) > fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_p)))
+                float area_p = fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_p));
+                float area_q = fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_q));
+
+                /* Rounding can leave nearly coincident control triangles
+                 * overlapping forever. Non-finite areas cannot be resolved
+                 * by subdivision either. The tolerance is in path units. */
+                if (!isfinite(area_p) || !isfinite(area_q)
+                        || (area_p < 1e-5f && area_q < 1e-5f))
+                    break;
+
+                if (area_q > area_p)
                 {
                     if (!d2d_geometry_split_bezier(geometry, &idx_q))
                         return E_OUTOFMEMORY;
